{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1795772771","published":"2026-11-27T09:46:32Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:43:47.975084149Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-55005","CVE-2026-106570","CVE-2026-116146","CVE-2026-116157","CVE-2026-119123","CVE-2026-130651","CVE-2026-130653","CVE-2026-130654","CVE-2026-130655","CVE-2026-130656","CVE-2026-130658","CVE-2026-130659","CVE-2026-130660","CVE-2026-130663","CVE-2026-130664","CVE-2026-130666","CVE-2026-130667","CVE-2026-130670","CVE-2026-86424"],"summary":"ImageMagick: Fix of 19 CVEs","details":"- Rebase to EPEL 9 ImageMagick-6.9.13.61-1.el9. Its tarball fixes:\n- CVE-2026-130651: stack overflow in the MSVG decoder\n- CVE-2026-130653: missing path policy check when reading MPC files\n- CVE-2026-130654: unauthenticated pixel data in the distributed pixel cache\n- CVE-2026-130655: crash in the BGR, CMYK, GRAY, RGB, YCbCr and YUV decoders\n- CVE-2026-130656: uninitialized memory disclosure in the MNG decoder\n- CVE-2026-130658: uninitialized memory disclosure in the RLA decoder\n- CVE-2026-130659: memory exhaustion from images with many profiles\n- CVE-2026-130660: heap over-read in the MVG decoder\n- CVE-2026-130663: filename injection in the MAGICK, XBM, XPM and UIL encoders\n- CVE-2026-130664: heap overflow in the pixel stream\n- CVE-2026-130666: resource limit bypass when reading XMP profiles\n- CVE-2026-130667: heap overflow when writing GIF images\n- CVE-2026-130670: heap over-read when importing BGRO pixels\n- Fix the index of the first pixel in the GIF encoder, broken by the\n  CVE-2026-130667 fix (upstream e830dbd2b)\n- First build for TuxCare 9.8 ESU, so this entry also lists the fixes that\n  earlier entries name: CVE-2025-55005, CVE-2026-86424, CVE-2026-106570,\n  CVE-2026-116146, CVE-2026-116157 and CVE-2026-119123\n- Drop the delegate, PerlMagick and distributed pixel cache backports that\n  the 6.9.13.61 tarball includes","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/t